        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The variable `Q13` is of type `float64` and appears to be categorical with codes 1.0 through 4.0, and some unlabelled codes 8.0 and 9.0 which I will treat as missing, as per standard practice when they are unlabelled and likely represent \"Don't know/Refuse to answer\".\n\nSince this is an election study, I will assume it relates to voting behavior/intent, thus making it a `behav_` variable. The label for `Q13` in the context of the full pipeline is missing, but based on typical survey structures, this might be about voting intention or political party support. I will assign a standard name and deduce the question label based on the context provided by the pipeline structure. Given the lack of explicit label in the input JSON, I will use a placeholder.\n\nStandard Name: `behav_vote_intent` (assuming this relates to voting)\nQuestion Label: \"Vote intention or party supported\" (Placeholder)\n\nStrategy: Categorical, map all known codes and treat 8.0/9.0 as `np.nan`.\n\nMapping based on assumed context (since the actual codebook entry was not provided in the prompt, only the input JSON structure, I will use the value counts observed):\n- 1.0 -> 'vote_party_a'\n- 2.0 -> 'vote_party_b'\n- 3.0 -> 'vote_party_c'\n- 4.0 -> 'vote_other'\n- 8.0 -> np.nan\n- 9.0 -> np.nan\n\nNow, I will write `surveys/eeq_2014/vars/Q13.py`.\n\n```python\n# behav_vote_intent — Vote intention or party supported\n# Source: Q13\n# Assumption: codes 8.0 and 9.0 treated as missing (unlabelled in data exploration)\ndf_clean['behav_vote_intent'] = df['Q13'].map({\n    1.0: 'vote_party_a',\n    2.0: 'vote_party_b',\n    3.0: 'vote_party_c',\n    4.0: 'vote_other',\n    8.0: np.nan,\n    9.0: np.nan,\n})\nCODEBOOK_VARIABLES['behav_vote_intent'] = {\n    'original_variable': 'Q13',\n    'question_label': \"Vote intention or party supported (Placeholder)\",\n    'type': 'categorical',\n    'value_labels': {'vote_party_a': \"Party A\", 'vote_party_b': \"Party B\", 'vote_party_c': \"Party C\", 'vote_other': \"Other/Undecided\"},\n}\n```",
